==English==

===Etymology===
Probably from {{bor|en|yi|שנויץ|tr=shnoits||snout}}, originally from {{der|en|de|Schnauze|t=snout, muzzle}}. The ''Oxford English Dictionary'' suggests the word may be pseudo-Yiddish coined in English. Attested since 1930.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɒzəl|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} The human [[nose]], especially one that is large.
#* {{quote-magazine|1932||The Passionate Plumber|Motion Picture||64|Buster Keaton is the plumber, passionate or otherwise, and he is more than ably assisted by the '''Schnozzle''', Jimmy Durante.}}
#* {{quote-book|1947|Leslie Waller|Show Me the Way||31|I poked that bastard in the '''schnozzle''', he told himself proudly, and everybody on the crew will thank me.}}

